From 9bcf55ac28006535f3e21b72e7665ed685754b9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kakarin <kakarin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:12:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(cockpit): let each browser turn the task console off

The phone-first Task cockpit appears automatically on remote hosts and in
viewports 720px wide or less. Owners running a desktop browser at a narrow
width had no way to suppress it: no config field, no settings control.

Add a per-browser preference (localStorage dsh-full-remote.cockpit, value
off) with two entry points, one settings switch and one Hide button in the
cockpit header. One controller per page keeps them in sync, storage events
cover other tabs, and the switch stays visible while hidden so the cockpit
can always be restored. shouldUseInteractionOverlay keeps its original
hostname/viewport rule.
